At a high level, the application follows a client-server architecture. The frontend communicates with the backend through REST APIs. The backend is built using Node.js and Express.js.

The backend handles requests, business logic, authentication and database operations. PostgreSQL is used for persistent data storage.

The AI/ML components are also hosted and integrated through AWS, so the backend can communicate with those services when required.

Finally, the backend sends the processed result back to the frontend through the API.
